## Agreed design decisions

| # | Decision |
|---|---|
| 1 | Customer-facing policies (Privacy Policy, Cookie Policy, Terms of Use) + default published agreements live as **single masters in `01 - SaaS default agreements`**, not in InfoSec. (Move keeps the file link valid; the InfoSec update-runbook path gets repointed; optional shortcut left in InfoSec for ISMS discoverability.) |
| 2 | **Marketplace (privacy-first) and SaaS (experimentation-first) are separate lineages** — kept in separate folders even while currently identical. |
| 3 | **Version unit = the whole contract package**, snapshotted together (not per-document). To change anything: copy the latest snapshot forward into a new dated folder and edit there. |
| 4 | Templates split by motion: **`01 - Microsoft Marketplace Template`** + **`02 - Customer Cloud Hosting Template`** (singular). All package content lives **inside dated snapshot subfolders**. |

## Snapshot naming convention

- `YYYY-MM-DD - LATEST` = active version · `YYYY-MM-DD - DRAFT` = work in progress · `YYYY-MM-DD` (bare) = superseded history.
- **Lifecycle:** `… - DRAFT` → finalize (rename to `… - LATEST`, drop `- LATEST` from the prior active) → superseded (drop suffix → bare date).
- **Invariant:** exactly **one** `- LATEST` per motion folder; zero-or-more `- DRAFT`; all others bare-date.
- Each motion folder carries a `_README` stating this convention + the copy-forward / never-edit-a-used-snapshot rule.

